%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: IntoAlftand
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268279254515749
    - rid: 4351268282100350976
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah- here we are.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268279254515750
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: What's up with the ruined shed over there?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351028
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I dunno. It's probably got something to do with the failed expedition.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... failed expedition?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351029
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, we're about to encounter the last bit of an expedition down into
      Alftand.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: What happened?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351030
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I don't remember exactly, all I know is that they've ran out of food
      and a Skooma-addict Khajiit went insane and killed a bunch of his fellows.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351031
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Khajiit? Skooma?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Telepathic Mantid?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The Khajiit are a race of cat people. Skooma is an addictive drug made
      out of a substance called Moonsugar.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351032
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Are you sure these bridges are safe?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351033
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, they're completely static objects in the original game, so we're
      gonna be fine.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Unless we do something stupid, but I don't think either of us is interested
      in that, are we?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I guess not.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351034
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351035
    - rid: 4351268282100351036
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: How is it chillier in here than outside?!?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351037
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Heat rises and cold falls? I dunno, Monika.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Monika looks around and seems to notice the splatters of blood all over
      the floor.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351038
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (That's a lot of blood...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Is all of this from that failed expedition?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351039
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yep.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351040
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: You're very nonchalant about this, {mc}.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351041
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I give Monika the stink-eye.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Oh yeah, it''s all: been there done that, for you ahaha...'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351042
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Sorry.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351043
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: No worries, Monika.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351044
    - rid: 4351268282100351045
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh yeah, there's gonna be hostile Dwemer machines coming up.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Dwemer? Like the people who made that lockbox back in the iceberg?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351046
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'That''s right: their technology is way more advanced than any of the
      modern people of Tamriel.'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351047
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Some of their advancements are even comparable to the technology from
      <i>our</i> world-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Which is pretty stinkin' impressive for a bunch of steampunkers in a
      fantasy world.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351048
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: If they're so advanced, why haven't they conquered everything? Are they
      really isolationist, or something?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351049
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: They were mostly isolationist for a while, if this underground citadel
      wasn't already indicitive of that-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351050
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But, during the First Era, that isolationist streak was broken after
      they discovered the Heart of Lorkhan.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: The thing Septimus thinks is behind the lockbox?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351051
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The very same!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351052
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, they attempted to use the power of the Heart to create their
      own mer-made brass god.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351053
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Which went so well that the entire race vanished from the face of Nirn.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351054
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... wow. That's certainly quite the tale about hubris...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351056
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah. There's a definite irony of narrative tropes materializing themselves
      in a world that literally depicts itself on some scrolls.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351057
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But, there are actual theories about how the Dwemer disappeared, and
      if they actually went somewhere.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Which is a topic for another day...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351055
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Perhaps in response to us talking about its former masters, a Dwarven
      Worker Spider attacks us.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351058
    - rid: 4351268282100351059
    - rid: 4351268282100351061
    - rid: 4351268282100351062
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351063
    - rid: 4351268282100351060
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Wow...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351072
    - rid: 1790118692274307142
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: A robot spider!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118692274307143
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... yeah? What's got you so excited about it?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118692274307145
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Are you kidding me? Of course I'm excited!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118692274307144
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: It's a miraculous piece of engineering; a fully automated worker bot!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118692274307146
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm pretty sure "the fully automated" part comes from the fact they trapped
      some poor thing's soul in there.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118692274307147
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351073
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Heh.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351074
    - rid: 4351268282100351076
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I turn toward Monika and place my index finger over my mouth, signaling
      that we have to be quiet.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351079
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: What's up, {mc}?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351077
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: (Shh... listen.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351078
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bdbdcd61e8bc6564f90148e30a6a1a14, type: 2}
    dialog: Where is it? I know you're trying to keep it for yourself, J'zhar...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351097
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bdbdcd61e8bc6564f90148e30a6a1a14, type: 2}
    dialog: You <i>always</i> try to keep it for yourself-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351081
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bdbdcd61e8bc6564f90148e30a6a1a14, type: 2}
    dialog: <NoiseText=3,1>No</NoiseText>!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351080
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bdbdcd61e8bc6564f90148e30a6a1a14, type: 2}
    dialog: There's got to be more skooma...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bdbdcd61e8bc6564f90148e30a6a1a14, type: 2}
    dialog: Shut up! <NoiseText=3,1>Shut up</NoiseText>!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bdbdcd61e8bc6564f90148e30a6a1a14, type: 2}
    dialog: Don't lie to me, J'zhar! You hid it! You always try to hide it from me!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Is that the skooma-addicted Khajiit?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351082
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: (Yep. It's best we sneak up on him and put him out of his misery.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351083
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351084
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Ehh... fair enough.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351086
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The two of us begin sneaking forward.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351087
    - rid: 4351268282100351088
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: With our target spotted, Monika draws back her bow.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351089
    - rid: 4351268282100351090
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Unlike the previous time we tried this, Monika doesn't stand back up
      once her bow is fully drawn.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: While it's a bit odd that she's gotten the confidence to this in just
      a few days...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 'Maybe we''re just operating under the Skyrim logic: she''s been leveling
      her skills enough to do this over the course of our time here.'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Regardless, Monika releases her arrow once she's sure it'll hit and-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360475574796410
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bdbdcd61e8bc6564f90148e30a6a1a14, type: 2}
    dialog: Grraah!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360475574796411
    - rid: 4351268282100351093
    - rid: 4351268282100351094
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Addict down.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351095
    - rid: 4351268282100351096
    - rid: 4351268282100351098
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351099
    - rid: 4351268282100351100
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: So, does this place have more to worry about than the little robot spiders?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351101
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, yeah.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351102
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, there's the Dwarven Spheres, which roll out into a sort of humanoid
      robot...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351103
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And there's the Dwarven Centurions, which are these large behemoth golem-kind-of
      guys.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351105
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And that's just the Dwemer-made stuff; there's also the Falmer to contend
      with.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: The Falmer?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351106
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Based on the name, are they another type of elves?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, yeah! I'm kind of impressed you made that connection.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351107
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: C'mon, {mc}, did you seriously forget I was smart?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351108
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: No! I'm just impressed you're keeping up with all this Tamrielic knowledge.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351109
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I can already imagine Natsuki rolling her eyes while Sayori spaces out...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: While Yuri takes notes?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, but this sort of thing's her shtick, so that'd be nothing out of
      the ordinary.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I guess you're right.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351110
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I wonder what they're getting up to at that magic school.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351111
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Something productive, I hope...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351268282100351112
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
